{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1350593843"}, "name":{"label":"BigPapaNoel"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-07-22T03:53:00-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"8.0.3"}, "id":{"label":"14333891380"}, "title":{"label":"No consideration for night workers"}, "content":{"label":"I am very frustrated because I work at night. My day begins at 7 PM. And I would like to know how many steps that I take while I’m at work. For people who work at night. Like I said my day begins at 7 PM and the following day does not begin until I go to sleep and wake up. This app resets at midnight. So I need to do manual math and order to break up and know what I’m actually walking during my active day and it’s frustrating because the app resets at midnight and I just can’t figure out the math. I know it sounds simple, but it’s really not. You need to update the app so people can have it reset at whatever time they want the app to reset at and it stays on that day.  For example, if I have Tuesday at 7 PM. Then all of my steps from 7 PM Tuesday to 7 PM on Wednesday should all be included for Tuesday.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=712286167&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id212308358"}, "name":{"label":"Retired_Marine_30_4"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-07-21T11:48:29-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"8.0.3"}, "id":{"label":"14331424377"}, "title":{"label":"No good now"}, "content":{"label":"Canceled because app\nNo longer works on iPhone 17 pro max ⭐☆☆☆☆\n\nThis app has become frustrating to use on a daily basis. It crashes often, interrupting use throughout the day, and the inaccurate step tracking makes it unreliable for keeping track of activity. The frequent bugs make even basic features difficult to use, and the battery drain is noticeable enough to affect normal phone use. It’s also a major battery drainer on the Ultra Watch, which defeats the purpose of using it for fitness tracking. On top of that, it constantly pushes paid features, which takes away from the overall experience. There are better, more reliable pedometer apps out there—I can’t recommend this one.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=712286167&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
